  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "結構動力學與耐震設計導論",
    "sub_ename": "INTRODUCTION TO STRUCTURAL DYNAMICS AND SEISMIC DESIGN",
    "describe_ch": "課程涵蓋結構動力學、耐震設計二大主軸，協助學生理解建築物在地震作用下的動態響應與設計對策，內容包括：單自由度系統、多自由度離散系統、反應譜與設計譜分析、設計地震力計算、地震分區規定、斷層帶與基地距離對設計的影響、既有建築物耐震能力的評估方法與案例解析等。透過理論講解與實務案例結合，課程強調訓練學生撰寫完整的結構計算書，並強化其耐震分析與設計實務能力。",
    "describe_eh": "This course is centered on two primary themes: structural dynamics and seismic design. It is designed to equip students with a comprehensive understanding of the dynamic behavior of buildings subjected to seismic excitation and the corresponding design methodologies. Core topics include single-degree-of-freedom (SDOF) systems, multi-degree-of-freedom (MDOF) discrete systems, response spectrum and design spectrum analysis, computation of design seismic forces, seismic zoning criteria, the influence of fault proximity and site-to-fault distance on structural design, as well as methodologies for seismic performance assessment of existing structures, supplemented by case studies. Integrating theoretical foundations with practical applications, the course places strong emphasis on the development of students’ abilities to produce rigorous structural calculation reports and to apply advanced seismic analysis and design techniques in professional practice.",
